    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41916" root="وسب" body-key="w">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَبَتِ الأَرْضُ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسِبُ</span>, (inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسْبٌ</span>,
TA;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اوسبت</span></b> ; <i>The land became abundant
in fresh herbage, such as is called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُشْب</span>, (S, K,)
<i>and in dry herbage.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسِبَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَوْسَبُ</span>,
inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَبٌ</span>, <i>He,</i> or <i>it, was dirty:</i> (IAar, K:)
syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَكِبَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشِنَ</span>. (TA.)

